# std - the CT standard library, published as a normal ct-pkg package.
#
# The repository root is the package root; the `std/` directory under it is the
# namespace root, so `-I vendor/std` resolves `import std::<mod>::<Unit>`.
#
# Version policy: 0.x means the surface may break in a minor bump. See README.md.
#
# `requires` is measured, not guessed. Literal receivers (`"/tmp/x".open("r")`,
# `"abc".len()`) are rejected by v0.19.1 with "method receiver must be a
# variable, an element, a call or a field chain", so 0.20.0 is the floor for
# that feature. `std::io` names its handle with a type alias
# (`pub type IoFile = struct ct_io_file;`), and type aliases only parse from
# 0.20.3 on, so 0.20.3 is the floor for the package as a whole.
#
# The version line restarted at 0.1.0; 0.1.0 also adds `std::io` (printf, puts,
# putchar, getchar, fflush, and file open/read/write/close) next to `std::num`
# and `std::math`. `-lm` rides in `ldflags` because std::math calls sqrt / fabs
# / isnan / isinf; on platforms where libm is part of libc it is a no-op, on
# the others it is required.
name = std
version = 0.1.0
licence = GPL-3.0-or-later WITH GCC-exception-3.1
requires = ct >= 0.20.3
ldflags = -lm
